description:
Part-time: 3 or 4 days per week

Remote, UK-based, with occasional travel

Salary: £40,000 FTE

£24,000 for 3 days £32,000 for 4 days

We are looking for an experienced, creative and commercially focused Marketing & Communications Manager to take ownership of our marketing across intelligence, technology and personal online protection services.

You will bring together the marketing of:
- B4 Secure - intelligence-led risk and resilience services;
- S.C.O.P.E. - our subscription threat intelligence platform;
- HALO - personal online protection for people in visible and high-profile roles;
- AI Synthesis - our technology company developing advanced AI and agentic AI capabilities.

This is a hands-on role for someone who can create and deliver a joined-up marketing strategy.

What you will do

You will:
- develop and manage one coordinated marketing plan across our businesses and services;
- create compelling written, visual and video content;
- plan, film and edit professional short-form video content;
- manage paid advertising campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, Instagram and other relevant digital platforms;
- manage and update our WordPress website;
- manage the S.C.O.P.E. subscriber portal through MemberPress;
- create landing pages, campaigns, email communications and lead-generation journeys;
- manage social media, SEO, website analytics and campaign performance;
- translate complex intelligence, security and AI services into clear, commercially powerful content;
- support product launches, thought leadership, events and business development.

What are we looking for

You will need:
- proven experience in marketing and communications;
- strong WordPress website-management skills;
- experience using MemberPress or another subscription or membership platform;
- demonstrable experience planning and managing paid digital advertising campaigns;
- strong video-content skills, including filming, editing and adapting content for different platforms;
- excellent copywriting and content-development skills;
- experience managing social media, email marketing, SEO and analytics;
- an understanding of lead generation, customer journeys and conversion;
- the confidence to work independently, bring ideas and take ownership;
- the ability to communicate complex or technical services clearly.

Experience within intelligence, security, technology, SaaS, professional services or business-to-business marketing would be advantageous.

Why join us?

This is an opportunity to shape the marketing function across two ambitious, founder-led businesses operating at the intersection of intelligence, organisational resilience and advanced technology.

You will work with an experienced intelligence team and support the development of new AI-led capabilities through AI Synthesis's partnership with the University of West London and Innovate UK.
